From da2c77e205fa6cf1bb1477fbfc5bfaff69470af8 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Latent <latent@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 10 Oct 2026 03:05:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Grain amount: blend the film's grain with the clean density
 (Latent)

Adds spk_params::grain_amount (+ grain_amount_set) and GrainParams.amount.
After the grain model has run, the developed density becomes
clean + amount * (grainy - clean): 0 no grain, 1 the model's own, more is
stronger. Unset or 1 skips the blend entirely, so every render is
byte-identical. The viewing glare that grain_active also turns on is not
affected. The film memo is not involved (it is bypassed whenever grain is on)
and the print memo hashes the film density's content.
Test: tests/test_grain_amount.cpp (13 checks).
---
